 | 2026-06-16 | 0.3.3 | **Abstention verdict** (epic #309 T2, `#311`). §8.2 adds the fourth verdict state `NOT ANSWERABLE BY THIS INSTRUMENT` to the MVP + calibrated lexicons and the verdict→token map (`ink-muted` — a measurement-scope condition, not `warn`/`alert`). When the deterministic answerability gate classifies the OEC as `out_of_scope` (long-horizon / network / novelty-decay), `verdictFor()` WITHHOLDS the ship/no-ship verdict as its outermost branch (precedes the `underpowered_design` flip and the numeric path); the score is still computed and `confidence_score` is never discounted (panel hard constraint). The withheld verdict carries its inspectable named reasons in a hairline-`rule` §7.7 note (message in `ink`, no semantic fill). No new colors/pills/icons. |
 | 2026-06-16 | 0.3.4 | **Input-lint disclosure surface** (epic #309 T3, `#312`). §8.2 codifies the degrade-and-disclose **disclosure note** as a sanctioned pattern: a non-verdict caution about the *input* (vague / leading prose, or a paraphrase-unstable pre-flight verdict) carried on `input_flags` and rendered beside the normal reading on the simulation detail page. It REUSES the §7.7 note anatomy verbatim — `0.75px` `rule` border, `paper-recessed` fill, message in `ink`, no semantic fill, no pill/icon — because it is a data caution, not an alarm. Unlike the 0.3.3 `out_of_scope` abstention it does **not** change the verdict label (the verdict is computed and shown normally); for the `abstain` state the note header reads "indeterminate — please clarify." No new colors/pills/icons; the lint routes and never discounts `confidence_score` (panel hard constraint). |
 | 2026-06-16 | 0.3.5 | **Answerable hypothesis authoring** (epic #309 T4, `#313`; the deploy-unblocker). The `simulations/new` wizard's `01 · Claim` section now defaults to four structured fields following the falsifiable template "If [change] for [cohort], then [OEC metric] [direction]," composed into the prose the API expects and shown verbatim in a `paper-recessed` mono preview; a quiet `Free-text instead →` toggle (§7.7 quiet control) keeps the escape hatch so terse expert claims are never over-constrained. The OEC metric picker (`05 · Outcome metric`) is **decoupled from A/B mode** — declaring a metric clears the answerability gate's `oec_undeclared` block in either mode (the paired lift delta stays A/B-only; single-arm reports the metric rate). Two new authoring surfaces REUSE the §8.2 / §7.7 disclosure-note anatomy verbatim — `0.75px` `rule` border, `paper-recessed` fill, mono label, body in `ink` (fixes in `ink-muted`), no semantic fill / pill / icon / alert-red: (1) a **live inline lint** rendering the deterministic zero-LLM `POST /simulations/preflight` answerability + leading-framing reasons/fixes as the user authors, and (2) the **needs_input surface** that catches the create path's `422` and renders the named reasons + fixes as guidance (never a dead-end), offering an explicit `Run anyway as generic reception` quiet affordance when `allow_override` (resubmits with `run_as_generic_reception`). No new colors/pills/icons; no migration; `confidence_score` arithmetic untouched (panel hard constraints). |
 | 2026-06-26 | 0.3.7 | **Fused PREDICTED/MEASURED citation lexicon + conversation chat** (#31 fusion, #32 multi-turn). §8.2 adds the experiment-memory chat's fused-citation source lexicon: `MEASURED · REAL EXPERIMENT` (a real recorded A/B outcome, §8.3 record) vs `PREDICTED · SIDIRA SIM` (uncalibrated simulated-agent agreement, explicitly `(uncalibrated)` per §8.3 — a direction/rank call, never an effect size; a prediction MISS is surfaced honestly, not smoothed). Both render in the **neutral** mono designator register (no semantic fill) and are categorically distinct from the §8.2 ship/no-ship verdict lexicon (still not rendered on `/memory`). The single-shot "Ask the archive" becomes a threaded conversation (§7.4 evidentiary-but-human prose, mono only for designators); per-answer citations; suggested follow-up chips reuse the §7.7 quiet/row-action control anatomy; streamed turns follow §9.4 reading choreography with the `prefers-reduced-motion` settled-frame fallback. No new colors/pills/icons; tokens only. |
 | 2026-06-16 | 0.3.6 | **Glanceable completeness checklist** (epic #309 T6, `#337`). §8.2 codifies a display-only `Completeness` block in the `simulations/new` manifest rail: an `N OF M ESSENTIALS` count rendered as a §8.2 panel-verdict-chip (mono, `paper-recessed` fill, `rule` border) over a per-item present/absent list in the §7.10 text-glyph register — present `✓` (`success`) + `ink` label, absent `·` + `ink-muted` label, each row prefixed with a mono `PRESENT`/`MISSING` word so color never carries state alone (§4.3 / §7.8). The six essentials (change · cohort · OEC metric · direction · conditional design attached · advisory mechanism) are derived **deterministically, zero-LLM** from the wizard's form state + the EXISTING live `POST /simulations/preflight` `reason_codes` (the "conditional design attached" item reuses the gate's own `structurally_invisible_change` signal rather than re-deriving the regime classifier client-side); the count is a human-glance number **never fed to `confidence_score` / the verdict / persistence** and **never gates submit** (the authoritative block/override stays in the T4 needs_input/`422` path). The lone advisory item (mechanism) is excluded from the count and mono-tagged `· advisory`. Frontend-only — no backend / no route / no migration. No new colors/pills/icons; `confidence_score` arithmetic untouched (panel hard constraint). |
+| 2026-06-26 | 0.4 | **Dual-color everywhere** (founder-signed; ticket #35, this PR). The dual-color aperture mark becomes the **standard mark on every surface — in-product nav and dashboard included** — replacing the prior "monotone in-product / dual-color brand-surfaces-only / never resting in the nav or dashboard" policy. §1.3 consolidated to two color states (static dual-color default + transient animation); §3 primary horizontal lockup repointed to the duo assets; §4.4 forbidden-`avira` list scoped to *standalone* accents only (the resting duo mark is exempt); §1.5/§11 asset roles updated (duo = standard, mono = fallback). The §9.2 aperture-close animation note is unchanged and still valid. RATIONALE: the founder chose visual brand consistency over the brand-vs-product split — one mark, one color story, on every surface. Code lockstep: `TopNav.tsx` (`SidiraLockup`→`SidiraLockupDuo`) and `AppShellV2.tsx` rail (`ConsoleMarkMono`→`SheetMarkDuo`) now render dual-color in-product. |
 
 ---
 
 When in doubt: re-read §1, §4.1, §8.1, and §9. The mark, the color
 architecture, the decision-rule primitive, and the settle-trace motion
 together carry the whole brand thesis.
diff --git a/frontend/components/TopNav.tsx b/frontend/components/TopNav.tsx
index cd9999ca..f341ce87 100644
--- a/frontend/components/TopNav.tsx
+++ b/frontend/components/TopNav.tsx
@@ -1,77 +1,77 @@
 "use client";
 
 import Link from "next/link";
 import { usePathname } from "next/navigation";
 import { useState } from "react";
 import AuthControls from "@/components/AuthControls";
-import SidiraLockup from "@/components/SidiraLockup";
+import SidiraLockupDuo from "@/components/SidiraLockupDuo";
 import { TOKENS, FONT_SANS, EASE_MECH } from "@/lib/design";
 
 // Workbench chrome — DESIGN.md §9.3 + R2 mock (product-mock-mvp.html).
 // MVP nav is Hypotheses · Library only; Objectives / Rollouts / Calibration
 // and the CAL readout are future-only surfaces and must not appear (R2.4 —
 // the nav never promises what the product can't do yet). Labels rename, the
 // routes underneath do not.
 const TABS = [
   { href: "/simulations", label: "Hypotheses", matches: ["/simulations", "/agents"] },
   { href: "/personas", label: "Library", matches: ["/personas"] },
 ] as const;
 
 export default function TopNav() {
   const pathname = usePathname() ?? "/";
   const [hovered, setHovered] = useState<string | null>(null);
 
   return (
     <header
       style={{
         height: 56,
         display: "flex",
         alignItems: "center",
         gap: 32,
         padding: "0 24px",
         borderBottom: `1px solid ${TOKENS.rule}`,
         background: TOKENS.paper,
       }}
     >
       <Link
         href="/"
         aria-label="Sidira home"
         style={{ color: TOKENS.ink, textDecoration: "none", display: "inline-flex", alignItems: "center" }}
       >
-        <SidiraLockup height={28} />
+        <SidiraLockupDuo height={28} />
       </Link>
       <nav style={{ display: "flex", gap: 24, flex: 1, alignSelf: "stretch", alignItems: "stretch" }}>
         {TABS.map((tab) => {
           const active = tab.matches.some(
             (m) => pathname === m || pathname.startsWith(m + "/"),
           );
           const hot = active || hovered === tab.href;
           return (
             <Link
               key={tab.href}
               href={tab.href}
               aria-current={active ? "page" : undefined}
               onMouseEnter={() => setHovered(tab.href)}
               onMouseLeave={() => setHovered(null)}
               style={{
                 display: "inline-flex",
                 alignItems: "center",
                 textDecoration: "none",
                 color: hot ? TOKENS.ink : TOKENS.inkMuted,
                 fontFamily: FONT_SANS,
                 fontSize: 13,
                 fontWeight: 500,
                 borderBottom: `2px solid ${active ? TOKENS.ink : "transparent"}`,
                 // §9.3: hover 80ms ease-out, tab underline 160ms mech curve.
                 transition: `color 80ms ease-out, border-bottom-color 160ms ${EASE_MECH}`,
               }}
             >
               {tab.label}
             </Link>
           );
         })}
       </nav>
       <AuthControls />
     </header>
   );
 }
diff --git a/frontend/components/v2/AppShellV2.tsx b/frontend/components/v2/AppShellV2.tsx
index 0bd6b9c8..810b6bb8 100644
--- a/frontend/components/v2/AppShellV2.tsx
+++ b/frontend/components/v2/AppShellV2.tsx
@@ -1,166 +1,170 @@
 // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 // AppShellV2 — the PRODUCTION v2 application shell (#372).
 //
 // The static /v2/* mocks render AppFrame with its MOCK defaults (6 href="#" nav
 // items + a mock workspace avatar). Production must NOT ship dead nav or fake
 // chrome, and must NOT mutate AppFrame's defaults (that would break the mocks).
 // So this shell composes the SAME visual frame from the shared v2 layer
 // (ConsoleShell scope + the .v2-appframe / .v2-rail* / .v2-appbar classes that
 // already live in styles/v2-theme.css and that AppFrame itself consumes) but
 // wires the REAL product chrome:
 //
 //   • exactly the two real destinations the global TopNav exposes —
 //     Hypotheses → /simulations (active on /simulations or /agents),
 //     Library → /personas — as real Next <Link>s with usePathname() active
 //     state. No href="#" dead items.
 //   • the rail footer renders the EXISTING AuthControls (Clerk org switcher +
 //     user button, or nothing when Clerk is off) — org-switching + sign-out are
 //     preserved, never reimplemented here.
 //   • title / provenance / actions pass through to the appbar, same as AppFrame.
 //
 // The whole subtree sits under ConsoleShell's `.v2-console` ancestor, so every
 // v2 token resolves. Token-driven only: no raw hex / rgb / font names here.
 // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 "use client";
 
 import type { ReactNode } from "react";
 import Link from "next/link";
 import { usePathname } from "next/navigation";
 
 import AuthControls from "@/components/AuthControls";
 import { clerkAppearanceConsole } from "@/lib/clerk";
 import { ConsoleShell } from "./ConsoleShell";
-import { ConsoleMarkMono } from "./Marks";
+// §1.3 (ticket #35): the dual-color mark is the standard mark on every surface,
+// in-product nav and dashboard included. The console rail brand mark uses the
+// duo aperture (SheetMarkDuo) — its fixed DUO_SID/DUO_AVIRA strokes render
+// identically on the dark console ground (no currentColor dependency).
+import { SheetMarkDuo } from "./Marks";
 import { ProvenanceMarker, type ProvenanceMarkerProps } from "./Provenance";
 // The shell owns the v2 stylesheet import so every production v2 page that uses
 // it inherits the `.v2-console` tokens + the .v2-appframe/.v2-rail*/.v2-sims-*
 // classes (ConsoleShell requires the page to import this sheet).
 import "@/styles/v2-theme.css";
 
 // The two REAL product destinations (kept in lockstep with components/TopNav.tsx
 // TABS). `matches` drives active state via usePathname(): Hypotheses owns both
 // /simulations and /agents, exactly like the global nav.
 const NAV = [
   {
     key: "simulations",
     label: "Hypotheses",
     href: "/simulations",
     glyph: "HYP",
     matches: ["/simulations", "/agents"],
   },
   {
     key: "personas",
     label: "Library",
     href: "/personas",
     glyph: "LIB",
     matches: ["/personas"],
   },
   {
     // Experiment memory (#28, #29) — retrieval over the past-experiment archive.
     key: "memory",
     label: "Memory",
     href: "/memory",
     glyph: "MEM",
     matches: ["/memory"],
   },
 ] as const;
 
 export type AppShellV2Props = {
   // which real nav section is current (matches a NAV key). Falls back to
   // pathname matching, but callers pass it explicitly for clarity.
   activeNav?: "simulations" | "personas" | "memory";
   // the page title shown in the appbar.
   title: string;
   // optional right-aligned appbar actions (e.g. the "New hypothesis" CTA).
   actions?: ReactNode;
   // optional single global provenance marker for the appbar.
   provenance?: ProvenanceMarkerProps;
   // content surface. "console" (default) = the dark Reading-Console body, for
   // pages reskinned to the v2 console language. "sheet" = a light reading
   // surface inside the console rail, for pages whose body still renders the
   // legacy ink-on-paper markup (a sanctioned Console-rail + Sheet-content
   // composition). The interim shell-wrap for the dense simulation pages uses
   // "sheet" so their dark-ink content stays legible until a full reskin.
   surface?: "console" | "sheet";
   // the page body.
   children: ReactNode;
 };
 
 export default function AppShellV2({
   activeNav,
   title,
   actions,
   provenance,
   surface = "console",
   children,
 }: AppShellV2Props) {
   const pathname = usePathname() ?? "/";
 
   return (
     <ConsoleShell>
       <div className="v2-appframe">
         {/* ── LEFT RAIL — persistent vertical nav, real destinations ───────── */}
         <aside className="v2-rail" aria-label="Primary">
           <Link href="/" className="v2-rail-brand" aria-label="Sidira Console home">
-            <ConsoleMarkMono size={28} />
+            <SheetMarkDuo size={28} />
           </Link>
 
           <nav className="v2-rail-nav">
             {NAV.map((item) => {
               const active =
                 (activeNav && item.key === activeNav) ||
                 item.matches.some(
                   (m) => pathname === m || pathname.startsWith(`${m}/`),
                 );
               return (
                 <Link
                   key={item.key}
                   href={item.href}
                   className={
                     active ? "v2-rail-item v2-rail-item--active" : "v2-rail-item"
                   }
                   aria-current={active ? "page" : undefined}
                   aria-label={item.label}
                 >
                   {/* active = 1px left ink bar (neutral, never signal) */}
                   <span className="v2-rail-bar" aria-hidden />
                   <span className="v2-rail-glyph v2-mono" aria-hidden>
                     {item.glyph}
                   </span>
                   <span className="v2-rail-label">{item.label}</span>
                 </Link>
               );
             })}
           </nav>
 
           {/* rail footer — the REAL Clerk org switcher + user button (or nothing
               when Clerk is off in dev). Reuses AuthControls verbatim so tenancy
               + sign-out behave identically to the legacy TopNav. Its own
               marginLeft:auto is harmless inside this flex-column footer. */}
           <div className="v2-rail-account-slot">
             <AuthControls appearance={clerkAppearanceConsole} />
           </div>
         </aside>
 
         {/* ── CONTENT COLUMN ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
         <div className="v2-appframe-content">
           <header className="v2-appbar">
             <h1 className="v2-appbar-title">{title}</h1>
             <div className="v2-appbar-right">
               {provenance ? <ProvenanceMarker {...provenance} /> : null}
               {actions ? <div className="v2-appbar-actions">{actions}</div> : null}
             </div>
           </header>
 
           <main
             className={
               surface === "sheet" ? "v2-appmain v2-appmain--sheet" : "v2-appmain"
             }
           >
             {children}
           </main>
         </div>
       </div>
     </ConsoleShell>
   );
 }
