   889	## 10. Refuse list
   890	
   891	These are never allowed to ship.
   892	
   893	- Purple / violet gradients of any kind.
   894	- Three-column "Built for X / Designed for Y / Trusted by Z" feature grids
   895	  with iconified colored circles.
   896	- Centered marketing-style hero blocks inside the application.
   897	- Gradient CTA buttons.
   898	- `border-radius: 9999px` pills, capsules, or fully-rounded controls.
   899	- The wordmark in lowercase.
   900	- The mark with gradient fills, drop shadows, bevels, or 3D effects.
   901	- The mark with arbitrary rotation outside the §9.2 animation keyframes.
   902	- The mark in any color other than `ink`, `paper`, or the sanctioned dual
   903	  Sid-blue + Avira-rose split.
   904	- Stock photography. Abstract blob backgrounds. Geometric mesh patterns.
   905	- "AI-shimmer" / pulsing-gradient loading states.
   906	- `system-ui`, `-apple-system`, `Inter`, `Roboto`, or `Helvetica` as a primary
   907	  display or body font in production.
   908	- "Made by humans" / "Powered by AI" footer badges.
   909	- **Glass surfaces anywhere except live computed readings** (no glass chrome,
   910	  nav, tables, cards, text content, or marketing).
   911	- **Decorative instrument marks** — any trace, tick, or band not bound to
   912	  backend data ("instrument cosplay — worse than no trace").
   913	- **A verdict chip without its decision policy** (§8.1).
   914	- **Spinners, progress bars, and skeleton loaders** — the trace is the
   915	  progress indicator; pending states are honest text (§8.6).
   916	- **Calibrated / Brier / isotonic UI before the backend computes it** (§8.3).
   917	- **Count-up / odometer numerals** — numerals fade in over the trace's final
   918	  120 ms (§9.1).
